,title,link,text,language,family
0,Chittagonian language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chittagonian_language,"Chittagonian is a member of the Bengali-Assamese sub-branch of the Eastern group of Indo-Aryan languages, a branch of the wider Indo-European language family. It is derived through an Eastern Middle Indo-Aryan from Old Indo-Aryan, and ultimately from Proto-Indo-European. [5]",Chittagonian,Indo-European
